  "result": "All 4 tests pass.\n\nI added `editor/buffer.py`, the only missing piece. It implements `TextBuffer` with insert, delete, undo, and redo, plus bounds checks that raise `IndexError` without touching the buffer. Undo and redo depth is unbounded, and any new edit clears the redo stack.\n\nI chose Approach A, the command pattern. Each edit stores only its position and the affected substring, so its inverse is trivial to compute and memory scales with edit size rather than buffer size times history length, which matters for an unbounded history on a large buffer.",
